    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0343" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/9–2345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Council of People’s Commissars of
                        the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stalin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Truman </hi><anchor n="78" xml:id="d130-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-09-22">22 September, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I received your message.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d130-f2"/> I inquired Molotov, but
                    have not yet his answer. I became acquainted with the matter and came to a
                    conclusion that if the question relates to the participation of France and China
                    in the settlement of the Balkan affairs, these governments, according to the
                    exact meaning of the decisions of the Berlin Conference, must not be invited to
                    participate.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d130-f1" n="78" type="source" xml:id="d130-f1-content">
                <p>The text of this message was transmitted to the Secretary of State in White House
                    message No. 350, September 23, from Admiral Leahy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d130-f2" n="79" xml:id="d130-f2-content">
                <p>Reference is to the President’s message No. 346 of September 22, to Stalin, <ref
                        target="#pg328">p. 328</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
